From 6e9745c1115f27325b0d3126e2dfaeded810a7cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ali <ali.shahid003@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:46:15 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add soft-fail watch list: re-check D-band Solana coins that
 never get a KOL-triggered re-score

Real gap Ali flagged live: a D-band Solana token only gets re-queued for a
real re-score via _maybe_queue_rescan, which fires ONLY when a fresh MC
point arrives -- and the only source of MC points today is Layer 2's
tracked-KOL-wallet feed. A token no tracked wallet ever trades never gets a
second look, even if it quietly becomes structurally clean within its first
hours.

- state.py: new soft_fail_watch list (watch_add/get_soft_fail_watch/
  watch_remove/watch_touch), capped at 12h age / 300 items.
- layer0_scoring.py: free_recheck_solana_signals -- zero-MadeOnSol-budget
  recheck of top10 concentration + holder growth via the existing free RPC
  signals.
- scheduler.py: _handle_scored adds a D-band Solana token (no momentum
  override) to the watch list, and drops it once a real re-score clears
  the band. _run_soft_fail_watch_cycle sweeps the list every fast cycle
  (0 MadeOnSol cost) and only queues a real 3-call re-score once a free
  signal shows genuine improvement (top10 <=35% or holder growth >=10/hr).
- layer8_momentum_override.py: fixed a real pre-existing bug caught while
  testing this -- _parse_time only handled datetime/ISO strings, but
  state.py's real mc_history stores plain float epoch timestamps, so
  detect_momentum_override crashed on its first real call with actual
  recorded MC history (2+ points). Not hypothetical: this is the exact
  path scheduler._handle_scored's band-D branch hits live.
- 20 new tests (state + scheduler + the RPC-gate logic), all mocked, no
  real network calls. Full suite: 408 passed.

